@h1 Pipes h1@

Pipes — @@@code @name |slot| code@@@ — are the @strong only strong@ parameter
form that composes with a body. A pipe slot can sit on the opening line or
scatter through the body, and duplicate keys resolve last-one-wins. Reach for
pipes when a node has both parameters and content, or when you want to switch a
value partway through.

@aside(class note) 💡 Pipes are the noisiest form and the one prone to the greedy-bind trap below. Where you don't need a body, prefer @a |href /docs/guides/record-arg/| record-arg a@ or @a |href /docs/guides/colon-scatter/| colon-scatter a@. aside@

@h2 The slot grammar h2@

Each @@@code |…| code@@@ holds one slot, read with the shared parameter grammar:

@@@pre
@figure |src lamp.png| |full width!| |caption The second-order lens| figure@
pre@@@

That call passes a named @code src code@, a @code full width code@ flag (the
trailing @code ! code@), and a multi-word @code caption code@ value. The forms:

@ul
@li @strong Positional strong@ — one bare token: @@@code |full| code@@@
(fixture 06-parameters-pipes/bare-positional). Note @@@code |full| code@@@ is a
@em value em@, not a flag; a flag needs the @code ! code@. li@
@li @strong Named strong@ — @@@code |mood calm| code@@@ (basic-named); the value
may be several words (multi-word-value, multi-word-isolated). li@
@li @strong Multi-word key strong@ — @@@code |background colour - dark slate|
code@@@ splits on the spaced hyphen (hyphen-multi-word-key), while an embedded
hyphen with no surrounding spaces stays in the value: @@@code |well-known|
code@@@ (literal-hyphen-probe). li@
@li @strong Flag strong@ — @@@code |full width!| code@@@ makes a flag named
@code full width code@ with an empty value (flag-with-bang). li@
ul@

@h2 Open-line, scattered, and last-one-wins h2@

Pipes may appear on the opening line, or anywhere inside the body. When a key
repeats, @strong the last one wins strong@ — which is exactly what makes pipes
the form for switching a value mid-body.

@@@pre
@scene |mood calm|
The harbour was still.
|mood tense|
Then the bell rang.
scene@
pre@@@

Here @code mood code@ ends up @code tense code@ (fixture
06-parameters-pipes/last-one-wins; see also mid-body-scatter). You can also put
several pipes on one line:

@@@pre
@x |a one| |b two| |c three| x@
pre@@@

(multiple-pipes-per-line.)

@h2 Empty pipes and pipe-shaped prose h2@

An empty @@@code || code@@@ inside a body contributes no parameters
(06-parameters-pipes/empty-pipe). And ordinary prose that merely contains pipe
characters stays literal — Wit does not mistake it for slots:

@@@pre
The signal flag read red | white | red.
pre@@@

That renders as text (pipe-in-body-text).

@h2 The multi-line-value bug h2@

A newline @strong inside strong@ a single @@@code |…| code@@@ value does not span
lines — the pipe never closes and you get @code E_UNCLOSED_NODE code@ (fixture
06-parameters-pipes/multi-line-value). Keep each pipe value on one line; for a
genuinely multi-line value, use a @a |href /docs/guides/form-fill/| form-fill a@
body or a @a |href /docs/guides/record-arg/| record-arg a@ brace.

@h2 The greedy-bind hazard h2@

A @strong bodyless pipes call strong@ — one with no @@@code name@ code@@@ on its
line — greedily reads forward to the next matching close:

@@@pre
@card |title X|
@card |title Y| card@
pre@@@

The first call swallows down to the second's @@@code card@ code@@@ and you get
@code E_UNCLOSED_NODE code@ (verified). Fix it three ways: add an explicit
@@@code card@ code@@@, leave a @strong blank line strong@ after the call, or make
a bodyless pipes call the @strong last strong@ thing on the line.

@h2 Common mistakes h2@

@ul
@li Putting a newline inside @@@code |…| code@@@ (the multi-line-value bug). li@
@li Forgetting the @@@code name@ code@@@ closer on a bodyless call (greedy-bind). li@
@li Writing @@@code |full| code@@@ expecting a flag — it is a positional value;
a flag needs the trailing @code ! code@. li@
ul@

